<script lang="ts">import { onMount } from 'svelte';import { api } from '$lib/api';let status=$state<any>(null),error=$state(''),updated=$state('');const stateLabel=(state:string)=>({open:'Available',checking:'Being checked',complete:'Complete',validation_error:'Check failed',delivery_exhausted:'Needs owner review',importing:'Being imported'}[state]??state.replaceAll('_',' '));async function refresh(){try{status=await api('status');updated=new Date().toLocaleTimeString();error='';}catch(e){error=e instanceof Error?e.message:'Status is unavailable.';}}onMount(()=>{void refresh();const timer=setInterval(refresh,60000);return()=>clearInterval(timer);});</script>
<svelte:head><title>Assignment status · Voynich@home</title><meta name="description" content="Check whether Voynich@home is assigning volunteer tasks and review the service checks that protect submitted work."/></svelte:head>
<div class="page narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Development preview</p><h1>Assignment status</h1><p class="lede">This page reports whether the server can issue new volunteer tasks. The project keeps assignments off until it accepts the campaign’s scientific plan and the service is ready to run it.</p>{#if error}<p class="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{/if}
<section class="panel"><h2>{status?status.assignments_enabled?'New tasks are available':'New tasks are paused':'Checking for available work…'}</h2><p>{status?.reason??'Contacting the project server.'}</p><p class="small muted">Deployment stage: {status?.stage??'Unavailable'} · Last checked: {updated||'Waiting for a response'}</p><button class="secondary" onclick={refresh}>Check again</button></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Scheduled checks and backups</h2>{#if status?.health}<p>Scheduled result checks: <strong>{status.health.maintenance.healthy?'Current':'Unavailable or overdue'}</strong></p><p class="small">Last successful scheduled check: {status.health.maintenance.last_success_at?new Date(status.health.maintenance.last_success_at*1000).toLocaleString():'Not yet recorded'}<br/>Last verified backup: {status.health.backup.last_success_at?new Date(status.health.backup.last_success_at*1000).toLocaleString():'Not yet recorded'}<br/>Oldest result awaiting a check: {status.health.oldest_pending_check_age_seconds===null?'None':Math.ceil(status.health.oldest_pending_check_age_seconds/60)+' minutes'}</p>{#if status.health.maintenance.error}<p class="error">{status.health.maintenance.error}</p>{/if}{#if status.health.backup.error}<p class="error">Backup check: {status.health.backup.error}</p>{/if}{:else}<p class="muted">Loading service health.</p>{/if}<p class="small muted">A failed scheduled check stops new tasks at once. The server also marks checks unhealthy after 20 minutes without a successful run. Volunteers can still submit outstanding results, and a manual owner pause remains until the owner ends it.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Work queue</h2>{#if status?.queue?.length}<table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Tasks</th></tr></thead><tbody>{#each status.queue as q}<tr><td>{stateLabel(q.state)}</td><td>{q.count}</td></tr>{/each}</tbody></table>{:else}<p class="muted">No tasks have been published.</p>{/if}</section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Release checks</h2><p>Before the owner opens public assignments, the project must accept:</p><ul><li>Hosted task recovery and browser resource controls.</li><li>Configured account-provider flows.</li><li>Restoration from a hosted backup.</li><li>Release rollback in the hosted environment.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome/blob/cbbaf5f136d281e70646f2b4ccc8d946401435a3/docs/RELEASE-STATUS.md">Review the release-check evidence ↗</a></section>
<details><summary>View the operating budget</summary><p class="small muted">The initial target is $10 per month. Before assigning a task, the server reserves part of its monthly checking allowance. Actual replay time and hosting costs still need measurement. Application limits cannot cap spending at the hosting provider.</p></details></div>
